In the hex format

;; if you want to print double words at a time
;; --format x is essentially your format specifier
x -s8 -fx -c24 0xffffff8000955db0

;; This will produce the hexdump that offline parsers can postprocessk
x -s4 -fx -c8192 0xffffff809a431db0 --force


Print in hex:
(lldb) type format add --format hex short
(lldb) type format add --format hex long
(lldb) type format add --format hex char
(lldb) type format add --format hex int
(lldb) type format add --format hex uint
(lldb) type format add --format hex uint32_t
(lldb) type format add --format hex uint64_t
